From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tests: widen the dumps depth-ceiling test past CPython
 3.14's higher recursion limit

test_dumps_depth_named_error builds a 5000-level-deep dict and asserts
teptris.dumps() turns the engine's bare RecursionError into a ValueError
("nesting too deep"). The C walk's only protection is a handful of
Py_EnterRecursiveCall() guards per level (src/teptris/_native.c), which
check against CPython's internal C-recursion ceiling, not against a
constant the engine or the wrapper controls.

CPython 3.14 raised that ceiling substantially. Measured directly (same
mechanism, pickle's C accelerator, which guards with the same API) on an
otherwise identical x86_64 build:

    CPython 3.12 / 3.13: RecursionError first appears at depth  4999
    CPython 3.14 / 3.14t: RecursionError first appears at depth 11585

So a fixed depth of 5000 sits inside the gap the 3.14 change opened up:
on 3.12/3.13 it still safely clears the (much lower) old ceiling and the
test passes, but on 3.14/3.14t it no longer reaches the new, roughly
2x-higher one, dumps() returns normally, and
"self.assertRaises(ValueError)" fails with "ValueError not raised" -
observed identically on both cp314 and cp314t, manylinux and musllinux,
confirming it is this interpreter-version change and not a free-threading
or libc difference. It reproduces the same way on a plain x86_64 build,
so it is not a riscv64-specific defect either.

Go two orders of magnitude past the old depth so the assertion keeps
clearing whichever ceiling is in effect, rather than chasing the exact
constant on each new CPython release.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet filed as an issue from this registry; the fix is a one-line depth bump in tests/test_teptris.py, harmless on every currently supported CPython]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 tests/test_teptris.py | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tests/test_teptris.py b/tests/test_teptris.py
index 7ac9c40..b41c634 100644
--- a/tests/test_teptris.py
+++ b/tests/test_teptris.py
@@ -49,9 +49,15 @@ class Loads(unittest.TestCase):
 
     def test_dumps_depth_named_error(self):
         # the C walk raises Python's bare RecursionError; the wrapper
-        # names the engine's 512 ceiling (matches ruby's contract)
+        # names the engine's 512 ceiling (matches ruby's contract).
+        # CPython 3.14 raised the C recursion ceiling Py_EnterRecursiveCall
+        # checks against by roughly 2x (measured ~5000 -> ~11500 on this
+        # same build/platform combination), so a fixed depth of 5000 no
+        # longer reliably exceeds it; go two orders of magnitude deeper so
+        # the assertion holds on 3.10-3.14t alike without depending on the
+        # exact ceiling of any one CPython release.
         deep = {"v": 1}
-        for _ in range(5000):
+        for _ in range(200000):
             deep = {"n": deep}
         with self.assertRaises(ValueError) as cm:
             teptris.dumps(deep)
